<title>GREECE: Triaina, Aspis lead Greek money market funds in H1.</title>
<headline>Triaina, Aspis lead Greek money market funds in H1.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Triaina and Aspis Pronia were leading Greece's 31 money market funds in the first half of 1997 with year-to-date returns of 8.42 and 6.36 percent respectively, the association of institutional investors said.</p>
<p>Money market funds under management reached 3.092 trillion drachmas at end-June, up 37.41 percent since the beginning of the year and 4.78 percent on May.</p>
<p>Money market funds made up 57.45 percent of the mutual fund industry's total assets which rose to 5.41 trillion drachmas in the first half of 1997, an increase of 41.84 percent.</p>
<p>Greek money market funds are required to invest a minimum of 65 percent of their assets in money market instruments.</p>
